# Cluster SSH host (laptop)

From this Mac, every `ssh` / `scp` / `rsync` to the cluster is:

```bash
wc3013@torch
```

Never invent `torch-login-a-*.hpc.nyu.edu`, `torch-login-b-*`, or any
FQDN as the host the user types. The prompt `[wc3013@torch-login-a-1]`
is the node after login, not the SCP target.

Example:

```bash
scp wc3013@torch:/scratch/wc3013/longcat-video-tta/<remote> <local>
```
